@@ -0,0 +1,48 @@
+# The Daily Grind
+
+Static marketing homepage. Serve locally with `pnpm start` (statikk on port 11222).
+
+## Client-side performance monitoring
+
+`perf-monitor.js` (loaded at the bottom of `index.html`) measures how long user
+interactions take to render **new contentful updates** on screen. It is scoped to
+the elements marked with `data-perf`:
+
+| `data-perf` value | Element |
+| ----------------- | ------- |
+| `nav`             | the navigation bar (every link, plus the logo) |
+| `order-now`       | the hero "Order Now" button |
+| `seasonal-card`   | each "Seasonal Favorites" card (label = card heading / button text) |
+
+It also tracks **client-side view navigations** (`history.pushState` /
+`replaceState`, `popstate`, `hashchange`, Navigation API), using the browser's
+native Soft Navigations API when available and a heuristic fallback otherwise.
+
+### Entry types
+
+| `type`                        | Source              | `duration` means |
+| ----------------------------- | ------------------- | ---------------- |
+| `next-paint`                  | Event Timing API    | input → next paint (with `inputDelay`, `processingTime`, `presentationDelay`) |
+| `interaction`                 | heuristic           | input → first frame that paints new text/media added to the DOM |
+| `soft-navigation`             | native or heuristic | triggering input (or URL change) → contentful paint of the new view |
+| `interaction-contentful-paint`| native              | per-element contentful paint after a soft navigation |
+
+`outcome` on heuristic entries is one of `contentful-paint`, `timeout` (no new
+content within `data-perf-timeout` ms), `superseded` (another interaction
+started first) or `page-unload` (a full-page navigation happened instead, which
+is what the nav links do today).
+
+### Where the data goes
+
+* **DevTools** – every entry is a User Timing measure named `dg:<type>:<component>`
+  (Performance panel → Timings), with the full record in `detail`.
+* **In page** – `window.dgPerf.entries` holds the buffer; `window.dgPerf.summary()`
+  prints p50/p75/max per metric; `window.dgPerf.onEntry(fn)` streams entries.
+* **Collector** – set `data-perf-endpoint="https://…"` on the script tag and the
+  buffered entries are POSTed as JSON via `sendBeacon` whenever the page is
+  hidden or unloaded (`window.dgPerf.flush()` sends on demand).
+* **Console** – add `data-perf-debug="true"` or open the page with `?perfdebug`.
+
+If a future client-side view updates content in a way the mutation heuristic
+cannot see, call `window.dgPerf.contentUpdated()` right after mutating the DOM,
+or mark the view container with `data-perf-view`.
